We use <title> tag to write title
   Example ->  <title> MY FIRST WEBSITE  </title>

When we close any tag we end with ‘ /’  in starting of the tag . ex ->  </title>

We use <body> tag . it Contains the main, viewable content of the website.

<h1> used for heading 
There is h1,h2,h3… heading the size will be differes for every headings
   Ex -> <h1>   welcome   </h1>

<p> used to write paragraphs 
    Ex -> <p> In HTML, an HTML document is divided into two primary sections: the <head> (header) and the <body> (body). The fundamental difference is that the <head> contains invisible             metadata and configuration data, while the <body> contains all the visible content shown to the user </p>    this will print like a para

Example program till now:
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
           <title>My Web Page</title>
  </head>
    <body>
          <h1>Welcome to My Website</h1>
          <p>This is a paragraph of visible text.</p>
    </body>
</html>

The <br> tag is used to insert a single line break in a text block. It is a "void element," meaning it stands alone and does not need a closing tag (</br>).

The <hr> tag stands for Horizontal Rule and is used to create a thematic break between paragraph-level elements on a webpage. In visual browsers, it renders as a horizontal line running across the page. It is also void element

The <pre> tag stands for Preformatted Text. It is used to display text exactly as it is written in your HTML source code.

